<title>POLAND: Gorazdze to buy cement plant from NFIs.</title>
<headline>Gorazdze to buy cement plant from NFIs.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish cement maker Gorazdze SA has signed initial agreements to buy 60 percent in cement plant Groszowice Sp z oo, Gorazdze said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Gorazdze said it had signed an agreement to buy 33 percent of Groszowice from National Investment Fund Hetman (NFI) and 27 percent from 14 other National Investment Funds.</p>
<p>It did not give the value of the transaction or any other details and company officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Polish 15 National Investment Funds of the country's mass privatisation scheme manage about 500 middle-sized companies.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
